WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.080
- Hey guys, it's Justine.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.760
And today we are unboxing
the Traeger 885 Grill.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.820
I am so excited about this.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.110
I've actually been looking
into getting a grill.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.790
And this one is perfect
because not only can you bake,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.260
grill and smoke in it.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.260
You can connect it to wifi
and control it with an app.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.120
It's basically made for me!

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.080
A huge thank you to Traeger
for sponsoring this video

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.920
and sending us a grill to check out.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.810
Jenna, the top of this says

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.610
that two people will
required for assembly.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.443
- [Jenna] All right!

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.360
- All right, get those
assembly fingers ready.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.290
This is a wood pellet grill.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.890
And what makes this also different,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.410
than a lot of normal
grills, is you can take it

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.080
down to a very low temperature.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.290
But also take it all the
way up to 500 degrees

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.240
and you can control all
of this from your phone.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.620
You can also control it on
the grill too, but come on.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.960
If you can control it with
an app, why wouldn't you?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.830
There's a safety feature
that won't let you turn it

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.100
on with the phone.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.320
But you can control the
temperatures and turn it off.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.630
So they have a variety
of different "flavors"

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.320
of wood pellets that you can get.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.680
So the ones that we have here,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.200
Signature, this is a maple
cherry and an artisanal hardwood.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.410
And we've got a Hickory,

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.820
which is a natural flavored hardwood.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.840
And on the back, it'll show you what type

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.350
of things these are recommended for.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.180
So the Signature is pretty
much all across the board.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.030
Good for basically cooking anything.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.865
So the capacity on this
is, I can cook 10 chickens,

00:01:14.865 --> 00:01:18.973
seven rib racks, and nine pork butts.

00:01:18.973 --> 00:01:19.889
- [Jenna] We need more friends!

00:01:19.889 --> 00:01:20.800
- We are.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.100
Hello, (shouts) does
anybody want to come over

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.310
and have a pork butt?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.910
Uh, they also sent me a hat.

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.790
Oh, that's actually nice
because the sun's in my eyes.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.167
So they actually sent me three hats,

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.066
(laughs) which is great.

00:01:29.066 --> 00:01:29.917
- [Jenna] I think the black looks nice.

00:01:29.917 --> 00:01:30.750
- You think?

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:31.624
Time to unbox.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.457
- [Jenna] There's a tag on your hat.

00:01:32.457 --> 00:01:35.401
- Uh, yeah. This is fashion, Jenna.

00:01:35.401 --> 00:01:37.970
(upbeat country music)

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.670
Look how nicely this is packaged!

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.560
There's also a little secret surprise.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.470
This little box actually turns into

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.600
a little cardboard cabin house.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.300
And our little niece
loves cardboard boxes.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.040
So we're going to turn this

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.260
into a little cabin for her afterwards.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.800
This is the first time I'm
not going to recycle this.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.200
It's going to be recycled into a home.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.033
Is this in the shot?

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.460
This box says start here.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.560
So we're going to, we're going to do that.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.380
Oh my gosh it's a note!

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:07.860
From the CEO of Traeger Grills!

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:08.693
Jeremy.

00:02:08.693 --> 00:02:10.070
- [Jenna] Does everybody get that note?

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:10.907
- Yes.

00:02:10.907 --> 00:02:12.080
"I just want to thank
you for choosing Traeger

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.310
and letting us into your backyard."

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.143
You're here.

00:02:14.143 --> 00:02:15.921
You've infiltrated and I'm happy about it.

00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:17.760
So here's our assembly guide.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.990
They've given us all the
tools like I don't have to go

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.964
and hunt down some tools from my dad.

00:02:21.964 --> 00:02:23.910
(packaging rustles)

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.582
They've even put little cup holders

00:02:25.582 --> 00:02:29.080
for you to put your beverage of choice in.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.671
This is it.

00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:32.390
I like that it comes
pretty much put together.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.070
You basically only have to
put the sides on and the legs.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.950
And then you're off to the grilling races.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.310
That's cool because Traeger
even has a YouTube channel

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.850
that they have a bunch of recipes on.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.890
So I'm definitely going
to be checking that out

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.050
to get some grilling inspiration.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:46.883
Oh my gosh.

00:02:46.883 --> 00:02:48.360
There's more stuff inside of it.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.760
Oh, (gasps) whoa!

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.093
Everything is very nicely packaged.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.060
Um, is that English?

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.210
And the lever?

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.843
Oh, "Remove before use" okay.

00:03:01.558 --> 00:03:05.113
whoa! It's just like a
never ending surprise.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:11.310
It's cool cause this is
actually a convection grill too.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.060
So it will be able to
circulate the air and the heat

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.310
to get a nice even cook.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.240
And I love a good even cook.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.050
I think this is the point where I need

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.653
to look at the directions.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.836
It's that time now.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:27.336
(upbeat guitar strumming)

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.370
And setup is starting now!

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.170
Should we high five before we start, or?

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.740
We did, we did.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:40.770
We removed all the grill parts and stuff.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.280
Okay. Here's the legs.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.563
Let's flip this around and
lay it down and assemble.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.613
(music continues)

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:58.620
I'd say we lift this up and
we tighten up the screws.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.520
This is great, I'm so hungry.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.940
The unfortunate reality
is I still need to go

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.330
to the grocery store

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.020
to get the foods that
I'm going to be grilling.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.770
So I think grilling is actually
going to happen tomorrow.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.150
There's someone coming down the driveway.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:10.983
- Who?

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:11.980
- I'm unsure.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.172
Do you think they want to help us?

00:04:13.172 --> 00:04:14.005
- Is that our mom?

00:04:14.005 --> 00:04:14.838
- Is that our mom?

00:04:14.838 --> 00:04:15.671
Oh it is.
- That's our mom!

00:04:15.671 --> 00:04:16.930
- That's our mom, Mom's home!

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.910
So maybe she's going to
help us with the grill!

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:20.210
Go for it! Just go for it!

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.700
There's even wheels on this thing, look.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.170
This is like all terrain.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:27.060
So now, Jenna, we need to put this on.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.760
I'm going to need your assistance.

00:04:29.678 --> 00:04:31.250
It's in! Look at that!

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:32.083
- Woo!

00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:34.770
- You guys can tell that the
sun has now shifted slightly.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:36.600
We did a good job.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.930
Well look, no, this needs
to go somewhere too.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.513
This is our little side table.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.330
Well, it looks like
everything is all set up.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.860
I'm going to now sync this to the app

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.933
and do the rest of the setup process.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:53.190
(smooth country music)

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.070
Okay. It's time to name the grill.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.047
I've got it all connected.

00:05:03.047 --> 00:05:04.640
"Sir-Ribs-A-Lot?

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.080
Stoked on Smoke.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.660
Baby Got Brisket."

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:08.830
Shall I come up with a custom name?

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.663
- [Jenna] You can do custom?

00:05:09.663 --> 00:05:10.496
- Yeah.

00:05:10.496 --> 00:05:12.060
- [Jenna] What about iJust Grill?

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.930
- Oh, iJust Grill.
- (mumbles) (laughs)

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.810
Okay. We're going to do that.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:17.643
All right.

00:05:17.643 --> 00:05:19.300
"Welcome to the wood fried revolution,

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.300
for true grilling for,"

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.133
oh man, this is great.

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:22.960
Yeah, give me all the notifications.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.410
Send me everything.

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:25.957
We have to season our grill.

00:05:25.957 --> 00:05:28.330
"This is to be used on
the initial firing only."

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:30.093
We need to prime the auger.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.810
It's priming.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.643
Ignite.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.868
Oh my gosh, it's igniting.

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:40.750
(grill hisses softly)

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.620
This is our first ignition.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:45.773
We've got accessories.

00:05:45.773 --> 00:05:47.930
Look at this!

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.790
Fancy, look how professional.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:53.160
Goodness. We've got
Traeger barbecue sauces.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.724
We've got a grill cleaner, all natural.

00:05:55.724 --> 00:05:57.993
(surprised gasp) We need these.

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.133
Oh my goodness, look.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:02.470
An internal temperature guide.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:04.236
Magnetic tool hooks.

00:06:04.236 --> 00:06:06.280
More barbecue sauce.

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.150
Pork and Poultry Rub.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.931
Wow. This is so incredible.

00:06:10.931 --> 00:06:11.764
- [Jenna] Oh my god!

00:06:11.764 --> 00:06:12.738
- I smell it too.

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:13.571
- [Jenna] Smells good.

00:06:13.571 --> 00:06:15.560
- Oh, it smells like a campfire.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.213
Oh, it's starting to get warm.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.280
It's happening.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:21.430
Here's our grill cover.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.653
Oh yeah.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:29.433
We're up 82, 83 degrees.

00:06:32.188 --> 00:06:35.021
(music continues)

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:37.680
It is the next day.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.910
And we actually covered
the grill last night.

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.930
And good thing because
currently I'm in the East Coast

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.030
and there was a downpour.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:46.760
So the grill is protected.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.120
I have been inside preparing a feast.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.971
I've got steaks, I've got chickens.

00:06:50.971 --> 00:06:53.700
I've got cauliflower, broccoli, potatoes.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.430
I think I got something else as well.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.770
I'm also going to make chocolate
chip cookies for dessert.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.670
There's a bunch of recipes
that I've kind of followed

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.620
but I've sort of mix
and matched some things.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:02.453
And I'm gonna try to make all

00:07:02.453 --> 00:07:04.260
of these things at the
same time on this grill.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.660
There's so much space in this thing.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:08.000
So that kind of gives
us a real opportunity

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.680
to make a bunch of different things.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:10.880
At the same time.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.820
I'm also can use this internal
temperature for the chicken.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.423
Also gotta fill up my pellets.

00:07:15.423 --> 00:07:18.529
(pellets rattle)

00:07:18.529 --> 00:07:21.446
(music crescendos)

00:07:22.433 --> 00:07:23.940
Just got a notification
from the Traeger app

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:26.500
that my grill is pre-heated.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.257
Now we're going to put all
of this stuff on the grill

00:07:28.257 --> 00:07:29.904
and I just want to be
completely honest with you guys.

00:07:29.904 --> 00:07:32.120
I've never really done
much grilling in my life.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.850
So I don't entirely, a hundred percent,

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:36.430
know everything about grilling.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.182
So I'm not claiming to be an expert.

00:07:38.182 --> 00:07:40.090
But what's great is, with the app,

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:41.700
I feel like it's giving
me all of the knowledge

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.100
that I need to know.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.600
And you know what? You live and you learn.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.909
So today, you guys are witnessing history.

00:07:48.909 --> 00:07:50.717
(grill hisses)

00:07:50.717 --> 00:07:51.800
Woo!

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.150
Toasty!

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:55.010
I've got some of the rub on this one.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:55.980
And then on this guy,

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.930
I've got another one
of the barbecue sauces.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.210
So this chicken, I have a nice little

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:02.910
Italian seasoning marinade
that my mom actually made.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.960
So this is, uh, this one's for my mom.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.889
Got the chicken marinading

00:08:05.889 --> 00:08:08.840
in some of the Traeger barbecue sauce.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.050
These are some potatoes with
a little garlic seasoning

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.930
and some random butter that I found

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.580
in the fridge that looked kind of good.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:16.840
So I threw it on there.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.252
This is a Parmesan Broccoli
Cauliflower recipe that I found

00:08:19.252 --> 00:08:21.170
on the Traeger recipes.

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:24.496
I also threw some garlic
in there because why not?

00:08:24.496 --> 00:08:26.796
Oh my gosh our kabobs
too, I got so much food.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.783
Good luck, little buddies.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.193
Now we wait.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.760
(tense music)

00:08:41.186 --> 00:08:42.860
I just got a notification that my chicken

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:46.550
has reached the internal
temperature of 165.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:48.190
Grill probe 166.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.180
I was aiming for 165.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:53.260
So guess what guys, I'm going
to take a little peek at it.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.210
Look at this.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:56.400
Look at those little grill marks!

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.130
I think I should've put it this way.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.240
I feel like that's what
you're supposed to.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.346
I put it the wrong way.

00:09:00.346 --> 00:09:02.120
I just learned something.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.313
And so did you guys.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:05.830
You guys aren't done yet either.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.423
Everything is still cooking.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:09.980
I'm gonna give the chicken
a few more minutes,

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.270
just cause I like mine kind
of done a little extra.

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.630
And then we'll take them out.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.870
And then we'll kind of
monitor everything else

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.400
that's happening in here.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.473
And then we eat!

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:22.770
The chicken is ready.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:23.740
- [Jenna] It's probe-ably done.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:26.547
- It's, oh my gosh, ha!

00:09:26.547 --> 00:09:28.400
"It's probe-ably done."

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.600
This looks delicious.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:34.610
Okay. I'm going to put
this into this chicken.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:35.770
They get that temp.

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.440
(probe beeps)

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.772
Chicky.

00:09:38.772 --> 00:09:41.053
Okay, these are marinated ones.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.810
I think these actually might be ready.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:44.643
- [Jenna] It's hot!

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.410
- Oh my God, it's incredible.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:48.243
Oh, is that good!

00:09:48.243 --> 00:09:50.943
I think we're, like,
fricking ready, actually.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:52.913
We're set.

00:09:52.913 --> 00:09:54.920
(grill hisses)

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.730
I got a whole meal right here.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.113
Our potatoes are needing
a little extra care.

00:10:00.025 --> 00:10:00.858
- [Jenna] Those look good.

00:10:00.858 --> 00:10:02.460
- Yeah, those are pretty much good to go.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.315
Look at that.

00:10:03.315 --> 00:10:04.148
- [Jenna] It's very nice.

00:10:04.148 --> 00:10:06.320
- I know, presentation is everything.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:07.850
My feast is complete.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.542
Now it's time for a taste test.

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:12.280
Complete is a lie, because the
